{%- comment -%}
═══ Panel metrics ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Everything below is measured off the rendered 800×480 page, not guessed:

  LAYOUT_H  410  what `.layout` gets once the title bar and screen gaps are out
  RIGHT_W   252  the right column is pinned here. Its widest line — "Berkeley
                 Marina  61°F/58°F" at 16px monospace — needs 247, and that
                 column may not wrap, so the slack is deliberate; the column
                 can still grow past 252 if a city name ever gets longer, and
                 the left column, which can wrap, gives up the width.
  LEFT_W    472  780 − 32 (screen padding) − 24 (column gap) − RIGHT_W
  MONO      0.6  monospace advance in em. Exact, not rounded: 11 characters at
                 8px measured 52.81px, and 11 × 8 × 0.6 = 52.8.
  LINE      1.3  set explicitly on every row below so row heights stay
                 predictable instead of riding on the font's `normal`
  HEAD_H   1.2×  `.label` at its font size, line-height 1.2. It ships as
                 `inline-flex`, which lands it on a line box 2px taller than
                 itself, so the headings below are set back to `block` to make
                 this exact. The size is body + 3, held between 12 and 16: on
                 any ordinary day that is 16, exactly as before, but a heading
                 that outweighs its own list by two to one is spending the
                 column's last pixels on the least of what is written in it.
  SECT_GAP 5–10  `.trmnl .column` carries `gap: var(--gap)` — 10px, whatever
                 the type is doing. Overridden here to ride the body size at
                 0.65×, because a cramped day should not be spending 50px of a
                 410px column on air between six headings.
  LIST_GAP   16  the gutter between the columns of a multi-column plain list
  RAIL_H    312  the rail is fixed-format, so its height is arithmetic rather
                 than a fit — see the sum below. What it does not use is panel
                 the agenda can borrow before it starts shrinking, and on a
                 Sunday the departure board's whole 178px share of it is free
                 whatever else happens, because the board is not drawn.
  ROW_H       3  1px padding above and below each row, plus its 1px rule
  BOX_W   0.8em  the checkbox, which is sized in ems so it stays in proportion
                 to the line it sits on, plus the ROW_GAP after it
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign LAYOUT_H = 410 -%}
{%- assign RIGHT_W = 252 -%}
{%- assign LEFT_W = 472 -%}
{%- assign INDENT = 12 -%}
{%- assign ROW_GAP = 8 -%}
{%- assign ROW_H = 3 -%}
{%- assign LIST_GAP = 16 -%}
{%- assign LIST_MAX = 3 -%}
{%- assign GROUP_GAP = 4 -%}
{%- assign NONE = '' | split: ',' -%}
{%- assign SIZES = '16,15,14,13,12,11,10,9,8' | split: ',' -%}

{%- comment -%}-- The alert banner sits above the columns and takes its height
out of theirs, so the left column has to know how tall it got before it can
choose a size. The banner is Inter, not monospace, so its lines cannot be
counted the way the agenda's are; instead the alerts are packed by character
count against a deliberately mean estimate of what fits — 0.52em average
advance across the 738px the banner has. Integer division plus one is the ceil;
the slack lives in that mean advance and in the 22px of chrome, which is 2px
more than the box measures. A whole spare line on top of that was costing the
agenda a step of type on every rainy day for nothing. --{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign alert_items = rain_alert.alerts | size -%}
{%- if rain_alert.active -%}{%- assign alert_items = alert_items | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if alert_items > 3 -%}{%- assign alert_font = 12 -%}
{%- elsif alert_items > 1 -%}{%- assign alert_font = 14 -%}
{%- else -%}{%- assign alert_font = 16 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign alert_h = 0 -%}
{%- if alert_items > 0 -%}
  {%- assign alert_chars = 0 -%}
  {%- if rain_alert.active -%}
    {%- capture rain_text -%}{{ rain_alert.chance }}% chance of rain today in {{ rain_alert.city }}. Bring your umbrella!{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign alert_chars = rain_text | size -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- for alert in rain_alert.alerts -%}
    {%- assign alert_chars = alert | size | plus: 2 | plus: alert_chars -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- assign alert_cpl = 738 | divided_by: alert_font | divided_by: 0.52 | floor -%}
  {%- assign alert_rows = alert_chars | divided_by: alert_cpl | plus: 1 -%}
  {%- assign alert_h = alert_font | times: 1.3 | ceil | times: alert_rows | plus: 22 -%}
  {%- if alert_h > 82 -%}{%- assign alert_h = 82 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign budget = LAYOUT_H | minus: alert_h | minus: 4 -%}

{%- comment -%}-- The longest line in each plain list. It does not change as the
ladder walks, and the rail wants the same numbers, so it is measured once here
rather than nine times below. --{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign bd_count = birthdays | size -%}
{%- assign eom_count = 0 -%}
{%- if is_last_day_of_month -%}{%- assign eom_count = checklists.end_of_month | size -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign sun_count = 0 -%}
{%- if is_sunday -%}{%- assign sun_count = checklists.sunday | size -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign task_count = tasks | size -%}
{%- assign bd_widest = 0 -%}
{%- for item in birthdays -%}{%- assign n = item | size -%}{%- if n > bd_widest -%}{%- assign bd_widest = n -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign eom_widest = 0 -%}
{%- for item in checklists.end_of_month -%}{%- assign n = item | size -%}{%- if n > eom_widest -%}{%- assign eom_widest = n -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign sun_widest = 0 -%}
{%- for item in checklists.sunday -%}{%- assign n = item | size -%}{%- if n > sun_widest -%}{%- assign sun_widest = n -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign task_widest = 0 -%}
{%- for item in tasks -%}{%- assign n = item | size -%}{%- if n > task_widest -%}{%- assign task_widest = n -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%}
═══ The rail ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Weather, then one of two things, then whatever still fits.

The rail is fixed-format, so unlike the agenda its height is arithmetic rather
than a fit. Measured off the rendered page: a weather or train row is 27.8px,
the Berkeley Marina wind sub-line 15.6, the station header 19.6, a `.label`
19.2, and the rail's own flex gap 16. A weekday comes to 312 against 311.94
measured.

On a Sunday the departure board is not telling anyone anything — there is no
commute to catch — so it is not drawn, and the Sunday checklist takes its slot.
That is the better trade twice over: the chores are legible at a size of their
own, and the agenda gets back the eight rows and a heading that were crushing
it, which is most of why Sunday used to be the worst-set day of the week.

The board's absence is unconditional; the checklist taking its place is not.
The list has to hold a full line per item over there for the height below to be
exact, so an entry too long for 240px leaves the list in the column — as does a
Sunday with nothing else on it, since chores beside "Nothing on the docket!" are
a worse use of 472px than chores in it. Either way the rail is weather alone
and the day still reads; both need a checklist the current one is nowhere near.
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign rail_avail = RIGHT_W | minus: INDENT -%}
{%- assign weather_h = 19.2 -%}
{%- if weather.sf -%}{%- assign weather_h = weather_h | plus: 27.8 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if weather.oakland -%}{%- assign weather_h = weather_h | plus: 27.8 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if weather.berkeley_marina -%}{%- assign weather_h = weather_h | plus: 43.4 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign bart_h = 38.8 -%}
{%- assign train_count = bart | size -%}
{%- if bart_status == 'ok' and train_count > 0 -%}
  {%- assign bart_h = train_count | times: 27.8 | plus: bart_h -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign bart_h = bart_h | plus: 19.6 -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}-- Sunday keeps its checklist in the column on a day with nothing
else on it: a panel reading "Nothing on the docket!" beside a list of chores is
a worse use of 472px than just putting the chores in it. --{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign other_sections = events | size -%}
{%- if bd_count > 0 -%}{%- assign other_sections = other_sections | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if eom_count > 0 -%}{%- assign other_sections = other_sections | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if task_count > 0 -%}{%- assign other_sections = other_sections | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- assign sunday_in_rail = false -%}
{%- if sun_count > 0 and other_sections > 0 -%}
  {%- assign slot = budget | minus: weather_h | minus: 16 -%}
  {%- for rail_size in SIZES -%}
    {%- unless sunday_in_rail -%}
      {%- assign RF = rail_size | times: 1 -%}
      {%- assign item_w = sun_widest | times: RF | times: 0.6 -%}
      {%- assign item_w = RF | times: 0.8 | plus: ROW_GAP | plus: item_w -%}
      {%- if item_w <= rail_avail -%}
        {%- assign rden = item_w | plus: LIST_GAP -%}
        {%- assign rcols = rail_avail | plus: LIST_GAP | divided_by: rden | floor -%}
        {%- if rcols > LIST_MAX -%}{%- assign rcols = LIST_MAX -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if rcols > sun_count -%}{%- assign rcols = sun_count -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if rcols < 1 -%}{%- assign rcols = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- assign rhead = RF | plus: 3 -%}
        {%- if rhead > 16 -%}{%- assign rhead = 16 -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if rhead < 12 -%}{%- assign rhead = 12 -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- assign rrows = sun_count | plus: rcols | minus: 1 | divided_by: rcols -%}
        {%- assign need = rrows | times: RF | times: 1.3 -%}
        {%- assign need = rrows | times: ROW_H | plus: need -%}
        {%- assign need = rhead | times: 1.2 | plus: need -%}
        {%- if need <= slot -%}
          {%- assign sunday_in_rail = true -%}
          {%- assign sunday_font = RF -%}
          {%- assign sunday_head = rhead -%}
          {%- assign sunday_cols = rcols -%}
          {%- assign sunday_need = need -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endunless -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- assign rail_h = weather_h -%}
{%- if sunday_in_rail -%}
  {%- assign rail_h = rail_h | plus: 16 | plus: sunday_need -%}
{%- elsif is_sunday == false -%}
  {%- assign rail_h = rail_h | plus: 16 | plus: bart_h -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign rail_spare = budget | minus: rail_h | minus: 16 -%}

{%- comment -%}
═══ Fitting the left column ═════════════════════════════════════════════════
The panel is a fixed 800×480 with nowhere to scroll, so the type has to be
sized to the day's contents rather than the other way round.

The rule this replaces counted "visual rows" against one hard-coded character
budget — 30 in a tagged section, 38 without — and mapped the count onto a font
size. But that budget was calibrated at 14px and then applied at every size, so
at 10px, where two-thirds again as many characters fit on a line, it went on
counting wraps that no longer happened. The count stayed high, the font stayed
small, and the estimate kept justifying itself: a column with 200px of empty
space in it was being set at 8px.

So this fits instead of estimating. Monospace advance is exactly 0.6em, which
makes a line's character budget nothing more than the width left over after the
tag and time columns, divided by 0.6 × size; titles are then broken on spaces
the way the browser will break them. We walk the sizes down from 16px — level
with the weather, which is as large as this column has any reason to be — and
take the first one whose laid-out height actually fits. Wrapping to two lines
at a size worth reading beats one line at a size that isn't.

Type size is the *last* thing to give, not the first, so at each size the panel
spends its space before it spends legibility:

  1. on a Sunday there is no departure board, and the checklist has usually
     already taken its slot — see the rail's own note above;
  2. plain lists go multi-column, because "Shave" does not need 460px;
  3. section gaps ride the type size rather than sitting at a flat 10px;
  4. the End of Month list moves into whatever the rail still has spare, if
     that is what makes this size work.

Only when all of those have been tried does the ladder step down. Order does
not matter to the arithmetic, only the sum, so the plain lists are counted
together in one pass ahead of the event sections rather than in reading order.
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign left_font = 8 -%}
{%- for candidate in SIZES -%}
  {%- assign F = candidate | times: 1 -%}
  {%- assign CH = F | times: 0.6 -%}
  {%- assign line_h = F | times: 1.3 -%}
  {%- assign msg_h = F | times: 1.105 -%}
  {%- assign head_font = F | plus: 3 -%}
  {%- if head_font > 16 -%}{%- assign head_font = 16 -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if head_font < 12 -%}{%- assign head_font = 12 -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign HEAD_H = head_font | times: 1.2 -%}
  {%- assign sect_gap = F | times: 0.65 | round -%}
  {%- if sect_gap > 10 -%}{%- assign sect_gap = 10 -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if sect_gap < 5 -%}{%- assign sect_gap = 5 -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign body_h = 0 -%}
  {%- assign section_no = 0 -%}
  {%- assign eom_h = 0 -%}
  {%- assign cols_birthdays = 1 -%}
  {%- assign cols_eom = 1 -%}
  {%- assign cols_sunday = 1 -%}
  {%- assign cols_tasks = 1 -%}

  {%- comment -%}-- Birthdays, the two checklists and tasks are all the same
  shape: a heading over a run of plain lines, the last three carrying a
  checkbox. Walking them as one pass keeps the wrapping arithmetic in a single
  place. --{%- endcomment -%}
  {%- for pass in (1..4) -%}
    {%- assign items = NONE -%}
    {%- assign widest = 0 -%}
    {%- assign box_w = F | times: 0.8 | plus: ROW_GAP -%}
    {%- case pass -%}
    {%- when 1 -%}
      {%- if bd_count > 0 -%}{%- assign items = birthdays -%}{%- assign widest = bd_widest -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign box_w = 0 -%}
    {%- when 2 -%}
      {%- if eom_count > 0 -%}{%- assign items = checklists.end_of_month -%}{%- assign widest = eom_widest -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- when 3 -%}
      {%- unless sunday_in_rail -%}
        {%- if sun_count > 0 -%}{%- assign items = checklists.sunday -%}{%- assign widest = sun_widest -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- endunless -%}
    {%- when 4 -%}
      {%- if task_count > 0 -%}{%- assign items = tasks -%}{%- assign widest = task_widest -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endcase -%}
    {%- assign item_count = items | size -%}
    {%- if item_count > 0 -%}
      {%- assign sect_h = HEAD_H -%}
      {%- if section_no > 0 -%}{%- assign sect_h = sect_h | plus: sect_gap -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign section_no = section_no | plus: 1 -%}
      {%- assign avail = LEFT_W | minus: INDENT -%}
      {%- comment -%}-- "Shave" on a 460px line spends three per cent of it. A
      plain list is set in as many columns as its *longest* item can still hold
      on one line — which is why this needs no cramped-day switch: at 16px one
      column is all that fits, and the list only breaks into two or three once
      the type is small enough that a single column would be mostly margin.
      Every item being one line is what makes the height below exact. --{%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign col_den = widest | times: CH | plus: box_w | plus: LIST_GAP -%}
      {%- assign cols = avail | plus: LIST_GAP | divided_by: col_den | floor -%}
      {%- if cols > LIST_MAX -%}{%- assign cols = LIST_MAX -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- if cols > item_count -%}{%- assign cols = item_count -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- if cols < 1 -%}{%- assign cols = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- case pass -%}
      {%- when 1 -%}{%- assign cols_birthdays = cols -%}
      {%- when 2 -%}{%- assign cols_eom = cols -%}
      {%- when 3 -%}{%- assign cols_sunday = cols -%}
      {%- when 4 -%}{%- assign cols_tasks = cols -%}
      {%- endcase -%}
      {%- if cols > 1 -%}
      {%- comment -%}-- The browser balances the columns, so the section is as
      tall as its longest one: ceil(items / columns) single lines. --{%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign list_rows = item_count | plus: cols | minus: 1 | divided_by: cols -%}
      {%- assign sect_h = list_rows | times: line_h | plus: sect_h -%}
      {%- assign sect_h = list_rows | times: ROW_H | plus: sect_h -%}
      {%- else -%}
      {%- assign cpl = avail | minus: box_w | divided_by: CH | floor -%}
      {%- if cpl < 1 -%}{%- assign cpl = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- for item in items -%}
        {%- comment -%}-- greedy wrap; see the note at the event copy below --{%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign lines = 1 -%}
        {%- assign fill = 0 -%}
        {%- assign words = item | split: ' ' -%}
        {%- for word in words -%}
          {%- assign word_len = word | size -%}
          {%- if word_len > 0 -%}
            {%- if fill > 0 -%}{%- assign need = fill | plus: 1 | plus: word_len -%}
            {%- else -%}{%- assign need = word_len -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- if need <= cpl -%}
              {%- assign fill = need -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- assign lines = lines | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- if word_len > cpl -%}
                {%- assign over = word_len | minus: 1 | divided_by: cpl -%}
                {%- assign lines = lines | plus: over -%}
                {%- assign fill = over | times: cpl -%}
                {%- assign fill = word_len | minus: fill -%}
              {%- else -%}
                {%- assign fill = word_len -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- assign sect_h = lines | times: line_h | plus: ROW_H | plus: sect_h -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign body_h = body_h | plus: sect_h -%}
      {%- comment -%}-- Remember what the End of Month list cost, so the rail can
      be offered it below if the column runs out of room. --{%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if pass == 2 -%}{%- assign eom_h = sect_h -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- for section in events -%}
    {%- assign body_h = body_h | plus: HEAD_H -%}
    {%- if section_no > 0 -%}{%- assign body_h = body_h | plus: sect_gap -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- assign section_no = section_no | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- comment -%}-- The tag column is as wide as the longest tag in the
    section and no wider, so it holds its alignment whatever the vocabulary in
    tags.conf grows into. Tags are set at 0.85em: bold uppercase stays findable
    a step down, and subordinating the category to the event name is what buys
    the name its width back. --{%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign tag_ch = 0 -%}
    {%- if section.tagged -%}
      {%- for event in section.events -%}
        {%- assign tag_len = event.tag | default: 'Other' | size -%}
        {%- if tag_len > tag_ch -%}{%- assign tag_ch = tag_len -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- assign tag_w = tag_ch | times: 0.51 | times: F | ceil -%}
    {%- assign gutter = INDENT | plus: ROW_GAP -%}
    {%- if section.tagged -%}{%- assign gutter = gutter | plus: ROW_GAP | plus: tag_w -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- assign prev_tag = '' -%}
    {%- for event in section.events -%}
      {%- if event.all_day -%}{%- assign time_ch = 7 -%}
      {%- elsif event.end -%}{%- assign time_ch = 11 -%}
      {%- elsif event.start -%}{%- assign time_ch = 5 -%}
      {%- else -%}{%- assign time_ch = 0 -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign time_w = time_ch | times: CH | ceil -%}
      {%- assign cpl = LEFT_W | minus: gutter | minus: time_w | divided_by: CH | floor -%}
      {%- if cpl < 1 -%}{%- assign cpl = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign origin = '' -%}
      {%- if section.tagged and event.tag == 'Other' -%}
        {%- case event.source -%}
        {%- when 'the-commons' -%}{%- assign origin = 'The Commons' -%}
        {%- when 'rallysf' -%}{%- assign origin = 'RallySF' -%}
        {%- endcase -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if origin == '' -%}
        {%- assign headline = event.title -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- capture headline -%}{{ event.title }} @ {{ origin }}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%}-- Greedy wrap: fill a line word by word and start a new
      one when the next word will not fit, which is what the browser does. A
      word longer than the whole line breaks mid-word, because the title span
      carries `overflow-wrap: anywhere`. --{%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign lines = 1 -%}
      {%- assign fill = 0 -%}
      {%- assign words = headline | split: ' ' -%}
      {%- for word in words -%}
        {%- assign word_len = word | size -%}
        {%- if word_len > 0 -%}
          {%- if fill > 0 -%}{%- assign need = fill | plus: 1 | plus: word_len -%}
          {%- else -%}{%- assign need = word_len -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- if need <= cpl -%}
            {%- assign fill = need -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign lines = lines | plus: 1 -%}
            {%- if word_len > cpl -%}
              {%- assign over = word_len | minus: 1 | divided_by: cpl -%}
              {%- assign lines = lines | plus: over -%}
              {%- assign fill = over | times: cpl -%}
              {%- assign fill = word_len | minus: fill -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- assign fill = word_len -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- assign body_h = lines | times: line_h | plus: ROW_H | plus: body_h -%}
      {%- comment -%}-- A message is clipped to one line, so it always costs
      exactly one. --{%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if event.message and event.message != '' -%}
        {%- assign body_h = body_h | plus: msg_h -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.tagged and forloop.first == false and event.tag != prev_tag -%}
        {%- assign body_h = body_h | plus: GROUP_GAP -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign prev_tag = event.tag -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- comment -%}
  ─── Spilling into the rail ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Only once the column has genuinely run out. Shrinking the agenda while 98px
  of panel sits blank under BART is the thing this is here to stop, but moving
  a list across on a day that did not need it would be churn for its own sake —
  so promotion is tried only after this size has already failed, and only if it
  is what makes the size succeed.

  A checklist is the right thing to move: it is chores rather than schedule, and
  its lines are short enough to live in a 252px rail. The End of Month list is
  offered first because it is the shorter of the two. Nothing is promoted unless
  every one of its items still holds a single line over there.
  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
  ─── Spilling into the rail ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  What is left to place once Sunday has its own slot is the End of Month list,
  and it goes across only when the column has genuinely run out: after this size
  has already failed, and only if moving it is what makes the size succeed. A
  day that did not need it is left alone.

  It takes its own size over there rather than the agenda's. Chores are not
  schedule, and a step of type spent on them is a step the agenda keeps — which
  is the whole reason for moving the list.
  ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign promote = 0 -%}
  {%- if body_h > budget and eom_h > 0 -%}
    {%- assign trial = body_h | minus: eom_h -%}
    {%- if trial <= budget -%}
      {%- for rail_size in SIZES -%}
        {%- if promote == 0 -%}
          {%- assign RF = rail_size | times: 1 -%}
          {%- if RF <= F -%}
            {%- assign item_w = eom_widest | times: RF | times: 0.6 -%}
            {%- assign item_w = RF | times: 0.8 | plus: ROW_GAP | plus: item_w -%}
            {%- if item_w <= rail_avail -%}
              {%- assign rden = item_w | plus: LIST_GAP -%}
              {%- assign rcols = rail_avail | plus: LIST_GAP | divided_by: rden | floor -%}
              {%- if rcols > LIST_MAX -%}{%- assign rcols = LIST_MAX -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if rcols > eom_count -%}{%- assign rcols = eom_count -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if rcols < 1 -%}{%- assign rcols = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign rhead = RF | plus: 3 -%}
              {%- if rhead > 16 -%}{%- assign rhead = 16 -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- if rhead < 12 -%}{%- assign rhead = 12 -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign rrows = eom_count | plus: rcols | minus: 1 | divided_by: rcols -%}
              {%- assign need = rrows | times: RF | times: 1.3 -%}
              {%- assign need = rrows | times: ROW_H | plus: need -%}
              {%- assign need = rhead | times: 1.2 | plus: need -%}
              {%- if need <= rail_spare -%}
                {%- assign promote = 2 -%}
                {%- assign promote_cols = rcols -%}
                {%- assign promote_font = RF -%}
                {%- assign promote_head = rhead -%}
                {%- assign body_h = trial -%}
                {%- assign section_no = section_no | minus: 1 -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- assign left_font = F -%}
  {%- assign left_sections = section_no -%}
  {%- assign left_fits = false -%}
  {%- if body_h <= budget -%}{%- assign left_fits = true -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{% if alert_items > 0 %}
<div style="max-height: 20%; border: 1px solid black; border-radius: 8px; padding: 4px 12px; margin: 2px 8px 8px 8px; font-family: Inter, helvetica, arial, sans-serif;">
  <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 2px 12px; margin: 0; padding: 0; line-height: 1.3; font-size: {{ alert_font }}px; font-weight: bold;">
    {% if rain_alert.active %}
    <span>{{ rain_alert.chance }}% chance of rain today in {{ rain_alert.city }}. Bring your umbrella!</span>
    {% endif %}
    {% for alert in rain_alert.alerts %}
    <span>{{ alert }}</span>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}

<div class="layout" style="flex: 1;">
  <div class="columns" data-adjust-column-gaps="false" style="height: 100%; padding: 0 16px; gap: 24px;">
    {%- comment -%}-- A day so full that it will not fit even at the smallest
    size gets anchored to the top instead of centred, so what falls off the
    panel is the tail of the list rather than a slice off each end. --{%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="column" style="flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; height: 100%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: {% if left_fits %}center{% else %}flex-start{% endif %}; gap: {{ sect_gap }}px; overflow: hidden; font-family: monospace; white-space: normal; font-size: {{ left_font }}px; line-height: 1.3;">
      {% if left_sections == 0 %}
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; height: 100%; font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold;">
        Nothing on the docket!
      </div>
      {% else %}
      {% assign birthday_count = birthdays | size %}
      {% if birthday_count != 0 %}
      <div>
        <div class="label" style="display: block; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: {{ head_font }}px; line-height: 1.2;">Birthdays</div>
        <div style="padding-left: {{ INDENT }}px;{% if cols_birthdays > 1 %} column-count: {{ cols_birthdays }}; column-gap: {{ LIST_GAP }}px;{% endif %}">
          {% for birthday in birthdays %}
          <div style="padding: 1px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #999; font-weight: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere; break-inside: avoid;">{{ birthday }}</div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% comment %}-- The events pipeline hands us the left column's event sections
      already ordered, already non-empty, and already sorted within themselves. A section
      whose tag was declared `heading` in tags.conf carries its own heading and needs no
      tag on its rows; the rest share one "Events" section where the tag leads each row in
      a column sized to that section's longest tag, so the titles line up down the page. --{% endcomment %}
      {% for section in events %}
      {% assign tag_ch = 0 %}
      {% if section.tagged %}
        {% for event in section.events %}
        {% assign tag_len = event.tag | default: 'Other' | size %}
        {% if tag_len > tag_ch %}{% assign tag_ch = tag_len %}{% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      {% endif %}
      {% assign tag_w = tag_ch | times: 0.51 | times: left_font | ceil %}
      <div>
        <div class="label" style="display: block; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: {{ head_font }}px; line-height: 1.2;">{{ section.heading }}</div>
        <div style="padding-left: {{ INDENT }}px;">
          {% assign prev_tag = '' %}
          {% for event in section.events %}
          {% comment %}-- Within a tagged section a run of the same tag gets a little air
          above it, which separates the groups without spending a whole row on a heading.
          The tag also already names where a Commons event came from, so the `@ origin`
          suffix is only worth its width on untagged (Other) events. --{% endcomment %}
          {% assign origin = '' %}{% if section.tagged and event.tag == 'Other' %}{% case event.source %}{% when 'the-commons' %}{% assign origin = 'The Commons' %}{% when 'rallysf' %}{% assign origin = 'RallySF' %}{% endcase %}{% endif %}
          <div style="padding: 1px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #999; font-weight: normal;{% if section.tagged %}{% unless forloop.first or event.tag == prev_tag %} margin-top: {{ GROUP_GAP }}px;{% endunless %}{% endif %}">
            <div style="display: flex; gap: {{ ROW_GAP }}px; align-items: baseline;">
              {% if section.tagged %}<span style="flex: 0 0 {{ tag_w }}px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: bold;">{{ event.tag | default: 'Other' | upcase }}</span>{% endif %}
              <span style="flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">{{ event.title }}{% if origin != '' %} @ {{ origin }}{% endif %}</span>
              <span style="flex: 0 0 auto; white-space: nowrap; text-align: right;">{% if event.all_day %}All day{% else %}{{ event.start }}{% if event.end %}&ndash;{{ event.end }}{% endif %}{% endif %}</span>
            </div>
            {% if event.message and event.message != '' %}
            <div style="padding-left: {% if section.tagged %}{{ tag_w | plus: ROW_GAP }}{% else %}{{ INDENT }}{% endif %}px; font-size: 0.85em; font-style: italic; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap;">{{ event.message }}</div>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
          {% assign prev_tag = event.tag %}
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
      {% if eom_count != 0 and promote != 2 %}
      <div>
        <div class="label" style="display: block; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: {{ head_font }}px; line-height: 1.2;">End of Month Checklist</div>
        <div style="padding-left: {{ INDENT }}px;{% if cols_eom > 1 %} column-count: {{ cols_eom }}; column-gap: {{ LIST_GAP }}px;{% endif %}">
          {% for item in checklists.end_of_month %}
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: {{ ROW_GAP }}px; padding: 1px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #999; font-weight: normal; break-inside: avoid;">
            <span style="display: inline-block; box-sizing: border-box; width: 0.8em; height: 0.8em; border: 0.13em solid black; border-radius: 0.13em; flex-shrink: 0; align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 0.3em;"></span>
            <span style="flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">{{ item }}</span>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% unless sunday_in_rail %}
      {% if sun_count != 0 %}
      <div>
        <div class="label" style="display: block; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: {{ head_font }}px; line-height: 1.2;">Sunday Checklist</div>
        <div style="padding-left: {{ INDENT }}px;{% if cols_sunday > 1 %} column-count: {{ cols_sunday }}; column-gap: {{ LIST_GAP }}px;{% endif %}">
          {% for item in checklists.sunday %}
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: {{ ROW_GAP }}px; padding: 1px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #999; font-weight: normal; break-inside: avoid;">
            <span style="display: inline-block; box-sizing: border-box; width: 0.8em; height: 0.8em; border: 0.13em solid black; border-radius: 0.13em; flex-shrink: 0; align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 0.3em;"></span>
            <span style="flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">{{ item }}</span>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% endunless %}
      {% if task_count != 0 %}
      <div>
        <div class="label" style="display: block; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: {{ head_font }}px; line-height: 1.2;">Tasks</div>
        <div style="padding-left: {{ INDENT }}px;{% if cols_tasks > 1 %} column-count: {{ cols_tasks }}; column-gap: {{ LIST_GAP }}px;{% endif %}">
          {% for task in tasks %}
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: {{ ROW_GAP }}px; padding: 1px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #999; font-weight: normal; break-inside: avoid;">
            <span style="display: inline-block; box-sizing: border-box; width: 0.8em; height: 0.8em; border: 0.13em solid black; border-radius: 0.13em; flex-shrink: 0; align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 0.3em;"></span>
            <span style="flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">{{ task }}</span>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}-- The right column is fixed-format and cannot wrap, so it
    takes the width it needs and the left column, which can wrap, takes what is
    left. Pinning it the other way round — a share of the panel each — is what
    left 26px stranded in a column that had no use for them. --{%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="column" style="flex: 0 0 auto; width: auto; min-width: 252px; height: 100%; display: flex; white-space: nowrap; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; gap: 16px; font-family: monospace; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.3;">
      <div>
        {% comment %}-- UV rides on the Weather heading rather than taking a row of its
        own: it is a single number, and the heading line is already half empty. --{% endcomment %}
        <div class="label" style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 16px; margin: 0; padding: 0; line-height: 1.2;">
          <span>Weather</span>
          {% if weather.uv %}<span style="font-weight: normal;">UV: <span style="font-weight: bold;">{{ weather.uv.max }}</span></span>{% endif %}
        </div>
        <div>
          {% if weather.sf %}
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; padding: 3px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #ccc;">
            <span>San Francisco</span>
            <span>{{ weather.sf.high }}&deg;F/{{ weather.sf.low }}&deg;F</span>
          </div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if weather.oakland %}
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; padding: 3px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #ccc;">
            <span>Oakland</span>
            <span>{{ weather.oakland.high }}&deg;F/{{ weather.oakland.low }}&deg;F</span>
          </div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if weather.berkeley_marina %}
          <div style="padding: 3px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #ccc;">
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px;">
              <span>Berkeley Marina</span>
              <span>{{ weather.berkeley_marina.high }}&deg;F/{{ weather.berkeley_marina.low }}&deg;F</span>
            </div>
            <div style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; padding-left: 8px;">
              Wind {{ weather.berkeley_marina.wind.dir }} {{ weather.berkeley_marina.wind.speed_kt }} kt{% if weather.berkeley_marina.wind.gust_kt %} (G {{ weather.berkeley_marina.wind.gust_kt }}){% endif %}
            </div>
          </div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% if sunday_in_rail %}
      {% comment %}-- Sunday takes the departure board's place. Nobody is
      catching a train to work, and the eight chores were the thing bending the
      agenda out of shape. --{% endcomment %}
      <div style="font-family: monospace; font-size: {{ sunday_font }}px; line-height: 1.3; white-space: normal;">
        <div class="label" style="display: block; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: {{ sunday_head }}px; line-height: 1.2;">Sunday Checklist</div>
        <div style="padding-left: {{ INDENT }}px;{% if sunday_cols > 1 %} column-count: {{ sunday_cols }}; column-gap: {{ LIST_GAP }}px;{% endif %}">
          {% for item in checklists.sunday %}
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: {{ ROW_GAP }}px; padding: 1px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #999; font-weight: normal; break-inside: avoid;">
            <span style="display: inline-block; box-sizing: border-box; width: 0.8em; height: 0.8em; border: 0.13em solid black; border-radius: 0.13em; flex-shrink: 0; align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 0.3em;"></span>
            <span style="flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">{{ item }}</span>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% unless is_sunday %}
      <div>
        <div class="label" style="display: block; margin: 0; padding: 0; line-height: 1.2;">BART</div>
        {% comment %}-- Sized to its own widest line — the two station names — rather
        than to a share of the column, which at 252px would have left the header a
        pixel of room. It reads as the narrower table either way. --{% endcomment %}
        <div style="width: max-content;">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; padding: 2px 0;">
            <span>19th St</span>
            <span>Montgomery St</span>
          </div>
          {% if bart_status == "ok" %}
          {% for train in bart %}
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 3px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #ccc;">
            <span>{{ train.depart }}</span>
            <span>&#10148;</span>
            <span>{{ train.arrive }}</span>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
          {% if bart.size == 0 %}
          <div style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; padding: 3px 0;">No trains</div>
          {% endif %}
          {% else %}
          <div style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; padding: 3px 0;">Unavailable</div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endunless %}
      {% if promote != 0 %}
      {% comment %}-- The End of Month list, which the column could not hold,
      taking the blank space at the foot of the rail rather than dragging the
      whole agenda down a size with it. Sized to the space it landed in, which
      is why it can sit a step below the agenda: chores are the thing worth
      spending that step on. --{% endcomment %}
      <div style="font-family: monospace; font-size: {{ promote_font }}px; line-height: 1.3; white-space: normal;">
        <div class="label" style="display: block; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: {{ promote_head }}px; line-height: 1.2;">End of Month Checklist</div>
        <div style="padding-left: {{ INDENT }}px;{% if promote_cols > 1 %} column-count: {{ promote_cols }}; column-gap: {{ LIST_GAP }}px;{% endif %}">
          {% for item in checklists.end_of_month %}
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: {{ ROW_GAP }}px; padding: 1px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #999; font-weight: normal; break-inside: avoid;">
            <span style="display: inline-block; box-sizing: border-box; width: 0.8em; height: 0.8em; border: 0.13em solid black; border-radius: 0.13em; flex-shrink: 0; align-self: flex-start; margin-top: 0.3em;"></span>
            <span style="flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">{{ item }}</span>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
Two right-hand sections rather than one: the ISO week, and where today sits in
the year. Both are `.instance`, which ships as
`flex: 1 1 auto; text-align: right` — sized for being the bar's only tenant.
Two of those split the slack and drift apart, and pinning them both to their
content instead leaves them packed against the title, because a flex line with
nothing that grows stays left. So every section here is `flex: 0 0 auto` and the
free space is handed to one `margin-left: auto` on the week: auto margins absorb
what is left only after flex-grow has taken its share, so this works precisely
because nothing grows. The trio then sits at the right edge as one block.

The rule between them is a span with no content and no width carrying a single
`border-left`, which puts the bar's own 10px `gap` on both sides of it. 18px is
the cap height of the 16px face plus a little, so the rule reads as tall as the
text rather than as tall as the bar.

The second section is drawn only when `day_of_year` is there. Template and data
deploy independently — the plugin to TRMNL, `update` to the host serving the
JSON — so the panel will at times be running one half ahead of the other. A
missing field would otherwise set "Day  ( To Go)" in the bar for as long as that
lasted; the guard falls back to the week alone, which is what the bar said
before, and takes the rule with it.

Widest realistic bar: "Last (Fourth) Wednesday, 30 September 2026" at 16px Inter
is ~354px, the two sections ~200px, chrome and gaps ~70px — about 625 of 800.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="title_bar">
  <img class="image" src="">
  <span class="title">{{ date }}</span>
  <span class="instance" style="flex: 0 0 auto; margin-left: auto;">{{ week }}</span>
  {%- if day_of_year -%}
  <span class="instance" style="flex: 0 0 auto; align-self: center; width: 0; padding: 0; height: 18px; border-left: 1px solid currentColor;"></span>
  <span class="instance" style="flex: 0 0 auto;">Day {{ day_of_year }} ({{ days_to_go }} To Go)</span>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
